1
00:00:01,802 --> 00:00:03,031
♪♪

2
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:39,884
Hi, Daddy. You're still up.

3
00:02:40,027 --> 00:02:42,394
Problems in Tokyo.

4
00:02:42,529 --> 00:02:44,555
Say good night, Kelly.

5
00:02:44,698 --> 00:02:47,190
- Now wait just a minute.
- It's okay, Jeff.

6
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:48,393
Just go.

7
00:02:48,535 --> 00:02:50,470
I'll call you in the morning.

8
00:03:04,985 --> 00:03:07,284
I thought we agreed you
were through with that loser.

9
00:03:07,421 --> 00:03:09,754
He's not a loser.

10
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:11,688
All right, he's a
money-grubbing snake.

11
00:03:11,825 --> 00:03:12,918
Stop it.

12
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,585
He loves me.

13
00:03:14,728 --> 00:03:16,128
Love. Love?

14
00:03:16,263 --> 00:03:18,596
He loves the fact that
your last name is Blake.

15
00:03:18,732 --> 00:03:20,633
Now, I don't want
you to see him again.

16
00:03:20,767 --> 00:03:25,671
He just asked me to
marry him, and I said yes.

17
00:03:28,508 --> 00:03:31,444
But I absolutely
forbid it, do you hear?

18
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:33,809
Kelly, come back here. Kelly!

19
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:45,786
Okay, $25 NASA.

20
00:03:45,926 --> 00:03:47,622
$10 greenies and birdies.

21
00:03:47,761 --> 00:03:50,060
Why don't I just give you
my car? It will be cheaper.

22
00:03:50,197 --> 00:03:52,942
Hey, I don't want to rush you guys,
but I've got to be out of here by 5, okay?

23
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:54,730
Taking Granny to
the theater again?

24
00:03:54,868 --> 00:03:57,337
What some people will
do to inherit a bundle.

25
00:03:57,471 --> 00:04:00,600
Yeah, Stan here earned his
money the hard way... he married it.

26
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:04,405
It's tough living off royalties from
books on the crisis in American ethics.

27
00:04:04,544 --> 00:04:08,003
Who knows? Maybe somebody
will make a musical out of it.

28
00:04:09,349 --> 00:04:10,681
All right, who's up?

29
00:04:10,817 --> 00:04:12,718
I believe you are, Mr. Blake.

30
00:04:12,853 --> 00:04:14,344
Stay away from my daughter.

31
00:04:14,488 --> 00:04:15,786
I love Kelly, and she loves me.

32
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,322
Don't give me that.

33
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:20,489
How much do you want?

34
00:04:20,627 --> 00:04:22,687
You think you can buy me off?

35
00:04:22,829 --> 00:04:24,661
You're not allergic to money.

36
00:04:24,798 --> 00:04:26,824
How does 10 grand sound?

37
00:04:26,967 --> 00:04:29,493
- Why, you dirty...
- Calm down, Jeff.

38
00:04:29,636 --> 00:04:32,231
Ellis, I think we'd
better get another caddy.

39
00:04:32,372 --> 00:04:33,372
Uh-huh.

40
00:04:33,473 --> 00:04:35,203
Think it over, Holden.

41
00:04:44,985 --> 00:04:46,920
<i>♪♪</i>

42
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:11,108
Come on in.

43
00:05:11,244 --> 00:05:12,872
<i>♪♪</i>

44
00:05:20,353 --> 00:05:21,514
Thank God.

45
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:44,039
Go next door and
tell him to turn it down.

46
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:46,544
Why is it always me?
Why don't you go?

47
00:05:47,981 --> 00:05:49,040
Fine.

48
00:05:51,651 --> 00:05:53,119
We'll both go.

49
00:06:03,797 --> 00:06:05,527
Mr. Holden?

50
00:06:18,078 --> 00:06:21,571
For the umpteenth
time, I didn't kill anybody.

51
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:24,651
I was driving back from a
golf tournament in Columbus,

52
00:06:24,784 --> 00:06:26,664
and I sure as hell didn't
shoot anybody tonight.

53
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:29,656
That's all I'm going to say
until my lawyer gets here.

54
00:06:33,693 --> 00:06:35,992
Well, speak of the devil.

55
00:06:37,264 --> 00:06:38,664
What the hell took you so long?

56
00:06:38,798 --> 00:06:41,393
It's the middle
of the night, Ellis.

57
00:06:42,769 --> 00:06:45,500
Ben, I'd like you to
meet Lauren Richmond.

58
00:06:45,639 --> 00:06:48,575
She's our new deputy D.A.
She'll be handling this case.

59
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:50,768
Lauren, Ben Matlock.

60
00:06:50,911 --> 00:06:54,211
Mr. Matlock, I can't tell
you what an honor this is.

61
00:06:54,347 --> 00:06:57,476
I've always thought that your
defense in <i>The People vs. Baker</i>

62
00:06:57,617 --> 00:07:01,850
was one of the most brilliantly
constructed and argued pieces of its time.

63
00:07:03,356 --> 00:07:07,760
<i>People vs. Baker</i> was 25
years ago, before you were born.

64
00:07:07,894 --> 00:07:09,954
I've read every
case you ever tried.

65
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,359
I did my junior thesis on you.

66
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:13,364
Hey, hey, what is
this? Happy hour?

67
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,560
Cut the crapola and
get me out of here.

68
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:19,139
Could I speak with
my client by myself?

69
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,740
Call me in my office.

70
00:07:31,017 --> 00:07:32,713
What's up?

71
00:07:33,753 --> 00:07:37,349
They think I killed this sleazy
little dirtbag named Jeffrey Holden.

72
00:07:38,591 --> 00:07:41,117
Tell me about this
sleazy little dirtbag.

73
00:07:41,261 --> 00:07:42,957
He was a caddy
at the country club.

74
00:07:43,096 --> 00:07:44,774
A couple of months ago, he
started dating my daughter,

75
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:46,096
but he was just after her money.

76
00:07:46,232 --> 00:07:48,997
The day before yesterday,
I offered him some.

77
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:52,697
I told him I'd give him $10,000 if
he'd break it off with my daughter.

78
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:54,398
Did he take it?

79
00:07:54,541 --> 00:07:55,804
No.

80
00:07:55,942 --> 00:07:58,776
No, no, he was
holding out for more.

81
00:07:58,912 --> 00:08:02,405
I can spot a
golddigger a mile away.

82
00:08:02,549 --> 00:08:04,484
Believe me, I wasn't
married twice for nothing.

83
00:08:06,386 --> 00:08:10,448
Well, anyway, the dirty little creep
got himself murdered last night,

84
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:13,583
and whoever did it used my gun.

85
00:08:14,928 --> 00:08:17,488
Oh, you own a gun?

86
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:20,498
This is America. Of
course I own a gun.

87
00:08:20,633 --> 00:08:23,398
I got a .22 in my
glove compartment.

88
00:08:23,536 --> 00:08:26,904
I guess they went
over it, did they?

89
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,509
Yeah, they're pretty sure
that's the murder weapon.

90
00:08:29,642 --> 00:08:32,082
I kept trying to tell them that
somebody could have stolen it,

91
00:08:32,212 --> 00:08:33,908
but they keep coming
back to the money.

92
00:08:34,047 --> 00:08:36,107
What money?

93
00:08:36,249 --> 00:08:39,811
Jeff Holden had a bunch of
money on him when he was found.

94
00:08:39,953 --> 00:08:41,751
$10,000?

95
00:08:41,888 --> 00:08:43,254
It's a setup, Ben.

96
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:47,259
I swear to you I have never been
anywhere near Jeff Holden's place.

97
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:50,463
Ben!

98
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:57,569
Well, where were you last night?

99
00:08:58,938 --> 00:09:00,497
I was driving back
from Columbus.

100
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:04,577
I'd been playing golf there all
day at Briarcrest Country Club.

101
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:08,079
They have this tournament
there every year, an invitational.

102
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,615
I don't suppose
you stopped for gas

103
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:15,211
or helped a pretty young
girl whose car had stalled

104
00:09:15,355 --> 00:09:17,153
or there's somebody
we could call?

105
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:18,622
I came straight home.

106
00:09:18,758 --> 00:09:21,284
I left at 6, and I get
in my house at 8:00.

107
00:09:22,328 --> 00:09:23,956
Nobody saw you?

108
00:09:24,097 --> 00:09:25,690
Not that I know of.

109
00:09:25,832 --> 00:09:29,428
Why does it always
have to be that way?

110
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:32,596
Ben, if I was going to kill this
guy... This Jeffrey Holden...

111
00:09:32,739 --> 00:09:34,059
Would I shoot him
with my own gun

112
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,860
and then put it in my
own glove compartment?

113
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,673
I'd have to be an idiot.

114
00:09:37,811 --> 00:09:39,837
I'm one of the wealthiest
men in the world.

115
00:09:39,979 --> 00:09:42,346
Do you think I got that
rich by being stupid?

116
00:09:44,784 --> 00:09:46,810
You never know.

117
00:09:57,864 --> 00:09:59,264
I can't believe it.

118
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:01,561
I'm going up
against Ben Matlock.

119
00:10:01,701 --> 00:10:05,729
I know what you mean...
Butterflies the size of basketball.

120
00:10:05,872 --> 00:10:08,569
Julie, you're just trying
to make me feel better.

121
00:10:08,708 --> 00:10:12,475
A distinguished lawyer like you
doesn't get nervous, but I'm a nobody.

122
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:14,205
You'll be just fine.

123
00:10:14,347 --> 00:10:16,839
Besides, it's just
a bail hearing.

124
00:10:16,983 --> 00:10:20,545
The only tricky part about a
bail hearing is staying awake.

125
00:10:20,687 --> 00:10:22,019
You'll be great.

126
00:10:22,155 --> 00:10:23,155
Thanks.

127
00:10:25,859 --> 00:10:28,055
All right. Let's get started.

128
00:10:28,194 --> 00:10:30,026
Your motion, Miss Richmond?

129
00:10:31,064 --> 00:10:34,523
If it please the court, the state
asks that bail be set at $2 million.

130
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:36,067
Two million dollars?

131
00:10:36,202 --> 00:10:39,832
Sir, only your attorney has the
right to speak, and it's not yet his turn.

132
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:41,464
Please be quiet.

133
00:10:41,608 --> 00:10:43,941
The defendant is a
man of immense wealth

134
00:10:44,077 --> 00:10:48,481
with far-flung business interests and
access to a virtually limitless capital.

135
00:10:48,615 --> 00:10:52,985
In the state's view, $2 million is
very reasonable and eminently fair.

136
00:10:53,119 --> 00:10:54,959
- You've got to be out of your mind.
- Ellis...

137
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:56,065
- That's enough.
- Ellis, don't.

138
00:10:56,089 --> 00:10:59,389
She makes it sound like all I've got
to do is walk up to a cash machine

139
00:10:59,526 --> 00:11:00,903
and $2 million will fall out.

140
00:11:00,927 --> 00:11:03,021
Mr. Matlock,
control your client.

141
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:08,397
Your Honor, may I have a moment to instruct
my client as to proper courtroom decorum?

142
00:11:08,535 --> 00:11:09,798
By all means.

143
00:11:09,936 --> 00:11:11,734
Shut up and sit down!

144
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:15,733
Thank you, Your Honor.

145
00:11:15,875 --> 00:11:18,435
I'll entertain your
motion now, Mr. Matlock.

146
00:11:18,578 --> 00:11:24,176
If it please the court, my
client is a wealthy man, yes,

147
00:11:24,317 --> 00:11:28,413
but he's also very much
a pillar of the community.

148
00:11:28,555 --> 00:11:32,014
His business is here. His
family is here. His friends.

149
00:11:32,158 --> 00:11:35,595
There's virtually no
risk of flight whatsoever.

150
00:11:35,728 --> 00:11:42,293
Bail should be set at...
$200,000 at the absolute most.

151
00:11:42,435 --> 00:11:44,768
Your Honor, the state
would like to point out

152
00:11:44,904 --> 00:11:49,933
that in this day of computers and fax
machines and satellite communications,

153
00:11:50,076 --> 00:11:52,944
Mr. Blake could run his
empire from anywhere.

154
00:11:53,079 --> 00:11:55,071
The risk of flight
here is enormous.

155
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,592
Your Honor...

156
00:11:56,616 --> 00:11:59,677
The court's motion granted.
Bail is set at $2 million.

157
00:11:59,819 --> 00:12:02,015
You're as crazy as she is.

158
00:12:02,155 --> 00:12:03,783
Excuse me?

159
00:12:03,923 --> 00:12:05,824
I didn't kill that bum.
Why would I run away?

160
00:12:05,959 --> 00:12:07,257
Give me one good reason.

161
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:09,453
Your client's not
listening to you, counselor.

162
00:12:09,596 --> 00:12:11,792
Get me out of here.
I have work to do.

163
00:12:11,931 --> 00:12:14,560
Maybe he just needs a
little time to compose himself.

164
00:12:14,701 --> 00:12:18,297
Twenty-four hours in
jail for contempt of court.

165
00:12:19,672 --> 00:12:23,074
Okay, sir, let me have your
watch, and let's empty your pockets.

166
00:12:27,347 --> 00:12:28,975
Okay, watch.

167
00:12:30,683 --> 00:12:31,683
Money clip.

168
00:12:34,053 --> 00:12:35,316
Wallet.

169
00:12:37,223 --> 00:12:38,384
What are these things?

170
00:12:38,524 --> 00:12:40,015
- Ball markers.
- What?

171
00:12:40,159 --> 00:12:42,094
- Ball markers.
- Okay, ball markers.

172
00:12:42,228 --> 00:12:44,595
Keys and change.
Anything else, sir?

173
00:12:47,867 --> 00:12:48,867
Ahh.

174
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:04,445
Hi. Fred Bigelow.

175
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:06,450
Just got here myself.

176
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:10,416
What do you want? The
top bunk or the bottom?

177
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:23,731
Okay, Sergeant.

178
00:13:38,584 --> 00:13:39,677
Hi, Bob.

179
00:13:39,819 --> 00:13:40,878
Hey, Conrad.

180
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:42,079
Where's Ben?

181
00:13:42,221 --> 00:13:43,245
He's busy.

182
00:13:43,389 --> 00:13:45,467
Is that the new assistant
D.A. Ben was talking about?

183
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:46,584
That's Lauren Richmond.

184
00:13:46,726 --> 00:13:48,627
- I hear she's good.
- Mm-hmm.

185
00:13:50,096 --> 00:13:51,621
So find anything interesting?

186
00:13:51,764 --> 00:13:53,475
Nothing that doesn't
fit the prevailing theory.

187
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:55,400
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

188
00:13:55,535 --> 00:13:58,596
Ellis Blake walked in here
and tried to pay Jeff Holden off.

189
00:13:58,738 --> 00:14:01,674
Jeff Holden either
refused or wanted more.

190
00:14:01,808 --> 00:14:03,743
Blake then pulled a
gun and killed him.

191
00:14:03,876 --> 00:14:05,572
And left all this money behind?

192
00:14:05,712 --> 00:14:08,409
Jeff Holden must have dropped
it when he took the bullet.

193
00:14:08,548 --> 00:14:10,483
It was all over the place.

194
00:14:10,616 --> 00:14:13,108
Mr. Blake just didn't
have time to pick it up.

195
00:14:13,252 --> 00:14:14,345
This guy was a caddy?

196
00:14:14,487 --> 00:14:16,649
I bet there are golf pros
that don't live this well.

197
00:14:16,789 --> 00:14:20,556
Lieutenant, I found this on the
ground just outside the back door.

198
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,059
It's a ball marker.

199
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:25,029
Golfers use them when their ball
is in the line of someone else's putt.

200
00:14:25,164 --> 00:14:27,531
Briarcrest Invitational,
dated yesterday.

201
00:14:27,667 --> 00:14:30,660
That's the tournament
Ellis Blake said he played in.

202
00:14:32,405 --> 00:14:35,375
I'm telling you it isn't mine.

203
00:14:35,508 --> 00:14:38,672
But you had ball markers
in your pocket the other day.

204
00:14:38,811 --> 00:14:40,622
Everybody else who was
at that tournament did, too.

205
00:14:40,646 --> 00:14:42,638
Hell, they were even
selling them for souvenirs.

206
00:14:42,782 --> 00:14:46,685
I wasn't there, Ben...
Not that night or any night.

207
00:14:46,819 --> 00:14:49,186
You act like you think I did it.

208
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:00,732
You're kidding.

209
00:15:00,867 --> 00:15:02,665
Jeff Holden was a blackmailer?

210
00:15:02,802 --> 00:15:04,668
Well, I checked his bank,

211
00:15:04,804 --> 00:15:11,176
and he had been making large
cash deposits for almost a year.

212
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:12,642
Maybe he was pushing.

213
00:15:12,779 --> 00:15:13,803
Maybe.

214
00:15:16,315 --> 00:15:17,578
Would you mind?

215
00:15:17,717 --> 00:15:19,481
Oh, I'm sorry.

216
00:15:20,486 --> 00:15:22,512
Then I checked with your bank,

217
00:15:22,655 --> 00:15:27,821
and you had been making large
cash withdrawals for almost a year.

218
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,826
Why would you
check with my bank?

219
00:15:29,962 --> 00:15:34,127
Well, I figure if somebody
was framing Ellis

220
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:35,701
that it had to be
somebody who knew

221
00:15:35,835 --> 00:15:39,795
that Ellis had offered
$10,000 to Jeff Holden.

222
00:15:42,809 --> 00:15:46,610
Ooh, boy, that was a nice shot.

223
00:15:46,746 --> 00:15:50,046
Actually, I hit it fat.

224
00:15:50,183 --> 00:15:51,412
Yeah?

225
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:55,345
What did...

226
00:15:57,190 --> 00:15:59,819
Jeff Holden have on you?

227
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:03,862
If you don't tell me now,
I'll ask you in open court.

228
00:16:06,766 --> 00:16:08,029
He had somehow found out

229
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:10,279
that the restaurant I'm
trying to sell in San Francisco

230
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:14,240
isn't exactly the financial
bonanza my books would indicate.

231
00:16:14,373 --> 00:16:15,864
Jeff said he could prove that.

232
00:16:16,008 --> 00:16:19,911
Since I was in no position
to call his bluff, I paid him.

233
00:16:21,347 --> 00:16:24,078
Well, do you have any idea
where you were that night?

234
00:16:24,217 --> 00:16:27,710
At my restaurant, cooking.

235
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:34,286
He had a tape of a
conversation that he and I had.

236
00:16:36,095 --> 00:16:39,395
Oh, you hit too far under it.

237
00:16:39,532 --> 00:16:41,763
What was in the conversation?

238
00:16:41,901 --> 00:16:43,164
It was about my grandmother.

239
00:16:43,302 --> 00:16:44,600
Oh, oh.

240
00:16:44,737 --> 00:16:46,968
The one who controls
all the money in the family.

241
00:16:47,106 --> 00:16:50,599
- I love my grandmother, Mr. Matlock.
- Yeah?

242
00:16:53,246 --> 00:16:56,341
Well, now you near
about hit it too high.

243
00:16:56,482 --> 00:16:58,280
Look here, how
about... Look here.

244
00:16:58,417 --> 00:17:01,080
No, look here. Now look. Look.

245
00:17:02,388 --> 00:17:05,552
Try to hit it just under
the square, right?

246
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:08,855
Just under the square and just
knock the fire out of that sucker.

247
00:17:08,995 --> 00:17:10,827
It'll go flying out of there.

248
00:17:10,963 --> 00:17:12,158
See there.

249
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:19,928
Well, these things
are hard to get out of.

250
00:17:20,072 --> 00:17:21,870
So you love your grandmother?

251
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:24,944
Yeah. It's just that she's
old and she's had a long life

252
00:17:25,077 --> 00:17:29,071
and now her health is failing,
so maybe it's just as well.

253
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:31,741
So it's time to
go to her reward.

254
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:34,547
I said that to Jeff Holden once,
and he said he could arrange it.

255
00:17:34,687 --> 00:17:36,365
Well, naturally I said
I wasn't interested,

256
00:17:36,389 --> 00:17:39,325
but then later on I found out he
not only taped the conversation,

257
00:17:39,458 --> 00:17:42,917
he edited it together to make it
sound like I asked him to knock her off.

258
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,896
Oh, and then he'd play
it to your grandmother.

259
00:17:46,032 --> 00:17:47,193
Oh.

260
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:50,462
The happiest moment of my life was
when I found out he was murdered.

261
00:17:50,603 --> 00:17:53,129
Oh. Where were you that night?

262
00:17:53,272 --> 00:17:56,265
Having dinner with
my grandmother.

263
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:59,709
It takes a lot of work to
inherit some money, doesn't it?

264
00:18:04,684 --> 00:18:06,880
Yeah, well, what
do you suggest now?

265
00:18:07,019 --> 00:18:09,955
Oh, I don't know. I don't
know anything about golf.

266
00:18:17,863 --> 00:18:19,798
Jeff Holden blackmailing me?

267
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,366
That's ridiculous.

268
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:24,959
Then all the money you're taking
out of the bank and giving to him

269
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:28,370
I guess is just a big tip, huh?

270
00:18:28,507 --> 00:18:32,103
What I do with my money
is my business, Mr. Matlock.

271
00:18:32,244 --> 00:18:36,011
You mean your wife's
money, don't you?

272
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,585
Excuse me.

273
00:18:39,719 --> 00:18:42,689
Your wife would cut you off at your
knees if she knew, wouldn't she?

274
00:18:42,822 --> 00:18:44,051
Knew what?

275
00:18:44,190 --> 00:18:47,285
About your affair with
Tom Neville's wife.

276
00:18:53,032 --> 00:18:56,594
Yeah, she'd cut off all your
money, she'd ruin your career.

277
00:18:56,736 --> 00:19:03,301
I mean, who wants to read books on
ethics by your garden-variety adulterer?

278
00:19:03,442 --> 00:19:05,377
What makes you think
I'm seeing Tom's wife?

279
00:19:05,511 --> 00:19:06,672
Ellis told me.

280
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:10,476
Things like this don't
stay secret too long.

281
00:19:17,957 --> 00:19:20,222
Jeff Holden had pictures.

282
00:19:20,359 --> 00:19:23,329
He said that he'd show them to
Tom unless I gave him money.

283
00:19:23,462 --> 00:19:25,022
But I didn't kill
him. I couldn't have.

284
00:19:25,097 --> 00:19:26,759
Why?

285
00:19:26,899 --> 00:19:30,301
Because I was with
Caroline Neville that night.

286
00:19:34,907 --> 00:19:39,072
This boy is blackmailing you, and
you're paying him to carry your clubs?

287
00:19:39,211 --> 00:19:42,147
You people are nuts.

288
00:19:42,281 --> 00:19:44,716
Now, look out
about that little ball.

289
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,910
- Strike there. Right here. See?
- Thanks.

290
00:19:47,053 --> 00:19:48,521
Just right there. Watch.

291
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:10,339
Here's your witness list.

292
00:20:10,476 --> 00:20:12,809
Lauren was supposed
to send that to my office.

293
00:20:12,945 --> 00:20:14,846
- She just forgot.
- Oh.

294
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:19,111
Lauren reminds me of me when I
started my first case against you.

295
00:20:19,251 --> 00:20:26,454
I was so overwhelmed and
determined and enthused and scared.

296
00:20:26,592 --> 00:20:28,083
Scared of what?

297
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,388
Of you.

298
00:20:29,528 --> 00:20:31,793
You are what scared me.

299
00:20:33,265 --> 00:20:36,064
Things are a little
different now, aren't they?

300
00:20:38,137 --> 00:20:41,801
Lauren says she finds
you very intimidating.

301
00:20:41,941 --> 00:20:43,705
She sure didn't act
it in the courtroom.

302
00:20:43,843 --> 00:20:46,779
She went right for my throat
and got what she wanted, too.

303
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,505
Beginner's luck.

304
00:20:48,647 --> 00:20:52,049
I just held my breath,
dove in, and prayed.

305
00:20:52,184 --> 00:20:54,085
I'm surprised you didn't
hear my knees knocking.

306
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:56,086
I was listening to my own.

307
00:20:56,222 --> 00:20:57,850
You? Never.

308
00:20:57,990 --> 00:21:00,152
I see Julie gave
you the witness list.

309
00:21:00,292 --> 00:21:03,990
It turns out there's one more
person to add. He just came forward.

310
00:21:04,130 --> 00:21:05,962
- Rob Barton.
- Who's that?

311
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:08,226
He lives across the street
from Jeffrey Holden's.

312
00:21:08,367 --> 00:21:11,064
He claims to have seen your
client at Holden's townhouse

313
00:21:11,203 --> 00:21:12,603
the night he was murdered.

314
00:21:21,547 --> 00:21:23,015
Okay, I lied. I'm sorry.

315
00:21:23,149 --> 00:21:24,378
What's wrong with you, Ellis?

316
00:21:24,517 --> 00:21:27,095
Why didn't you tell me you went
to Jeff Holden's house that night?

317
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,553
And give her more ammunition?

318
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:30,713
Besides, I didn't
think anybody saw me.

319
00:21:30,856 --> 00:21:32,757
Ellis, you can't
lie to me like that.

320
00:21:32,892 --> 00:21:35,092
I didn't kill him, damn it. I
went there to talk to him.

321
00:21:35,194 --> 00:21:38,039
I didn't even get up to the front door
before I turned around to go home.

322
00:21:38,063 --> 00:21:39,326
I never went inside.

323
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:40,865
All rise.

324
00:21:45,471 --> 00:21:46,837
Be seated.

325
00:21:48,507 --> 00:21:51,375
Miss Richmond, you
may call your next witness.

326
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:54,776
The state calls Lieutenant
Bob Brooks to the stand.

327
00:21:54,914 --> 00:21:56,815
Do you recognize
this gun, Lieutenant?

328
00:21:56,949 --> 00:21:58,747
Yes, I do. It has my tag.

329
00:21:58,884 --> 00:22:01,649
That gun is registered
to Ellis Blake

330
00:22:01,787 --> 00:22:04,416
and was found in the glove
compartment of his car.

331
00:22:04,557 --> 00:22:06,677
The bullet that killed Jeff
Holden came from this gun?

332
00:22:06,725 --> 00:22:08,159
Yes, ma'am, it did.

333
00:22:10,563 --> 00:22:12,555
Could you identify this for us?

334
00:22:12,698 --> 00:22:16,294
Yes. It's a ball marker
from a golf tournament.

335
00:22:16,435 --> 00:22:19,633
It was found on the ground
outside the decedent's town home

336
00:22:19,772 --> 00:22:23,038
about 4 feet from the back
door on the day after the murder.

337
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:26,475
Have you come across any others like it
in the course of this murder investigation?

338
00:22:26,612 --> 00:22:29,810
Yes. We found three just
like it in Mr. Blake's possession

339
00:22:29,949 --> 00:22:31,815
at the time of his arrest.

340
00:22:31,951 --> 00:22:33,510
Thank you.

341
00:22:33,652 --> 00:22:35,120
Mr. Matlock?

342
00:22:36,255 --> 00:22:37,917
No questions, Your Honor.

343
00:22:38,057 --> 00:22:39,582
The witness may step down.

344
00:22:39,725 --> 00:22:41,557
Why didn't you ask him anything?

345
00:22:43,696 --> 00:22:46,598
Because the more he
talks, the guiltier you get.

346
00:22:48,133 --> 00:22:50,068
Your Honor, may we approach?

347
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:58,905
Your Honor, I just learned that someone
with information relevant to this case

348
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:01,240
has come forward
and is ready to testify.

349
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,576
- I'd like to put him on the stand.
- Your Honor...

350
00:23:03,716 --> 00:23:06,880
Oh, I'm sorry to do this to Mr. Matlock,
and he has every right to object,

351
00:23:07,019 --> 00:23:08,819
but the witness is out
in the hall right now,

352
00:23:08,954 --> 00:23:10,699
and I don't know how
long he'll be available.

353
00:23:10,723 --> 00:23:11,723
But, Your Honor...

354
00:23:11,790 --> 00:23:13,301
If you would allow me to
call him now, Your Honor,

355
00:23:13,325 --> 00:23:14,725
I would have no
problem whatsoever

356
00:23:14,860 --> 00:23:17,056
with your then calling a
recess until tomorrow morning,

357
00:23:17,196 --> 00:23:20,257
thereby giving Mr. Matlock
ample time to prepare his cross.

358
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:21,697
Counselor?

359
00:23:26,305 --> 00:23:29,639
- Well, I guess I can live with that.
- Mm-hmm.

360
00:23:36,849 --> 00:23:39,546
The state calls Mr. Fred
Bigelow to the stand.

361
00:23:45,157 --> 00:23:48,127
That's the guy I was in
jail with. What's going on?

362
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:52,391
My name is Fred Bigelow, and right
now I'm living at the Downtown Hotel.

363
00:23:52,531 --> 00:23:55,763
Mr. Bigelow, I understand you
know the defendant Mr. Blake.

364
00:23:55,901 --> 00:23:59,167
That's right. He and I shared
accommodations recently.

365
00:23:59,305 --> 00:24:01,483
You were in a jail cell
together, is that what you mean?

366
00:24:01,507 --> 00:24:02,873
Yeah.

367
00:24:03,008 --> 00:24:05,307
You met the defendant
on the 24th of last month,

368
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:07,845
the day after Jeff Holden's
murder. Is that right?

369
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:10,279
Yes, that's when we
became cellmates.

370
00:24:10,416 --> 00:24:13,250
Mr. Bigelow, have you
been promised anything

371
00:24:13,385 --> 00:24:15,445
by anyone in the
District Attorney's office

372
00:24:15,587 --> 00:24:17,351
in exchange for your
testimony here today?

373
00:24:17,489 --> 00:24:18,855
No, ma'am.

374
00:24:18,991 --> 00:24:23,190
I'm here because I decided it was
my duty as a citizen of this fair city

375
00:24:23,329 --> 00:24:25,628
to come forward
with what I know.

376
00:24:25,764 --> 00:24:27,596
And that is?

377
00:24:27,733 --> 00:24:30,498
Well, we got to
talking in that jail cell,

378
00:24:30,636 --> 00:24:33,162
and being that he'd
never been in jail before,

379
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:34,534
he asked me for some advice.

380
00:24:34,673 --> 00:24:37,074
What kind of advice?

381
00:24:37,209 --> 00:24:40,941
Well, stuff like "Do you
keep your mouth shut

382
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,413
or do you tell your
lawyer you did it?"

383
00:24:43,549 --> 00:24:46,849
Of course, me, I told him, "Hey,
you don't admit nothing to nobody,

384
00:24:46,986 --> 00:24:49,615
especially if you're guilty."

385
00:24:49,755 --> 00:24:51,917
- You liar! I never said that!
- Ellis, sit down!

386
00:24:52,057 --> 00:24:54,177
I never said a word to you
the whole time I was there!

387
00:24:54,293 --> 00:24:55,761
- Quiet!
- Who bribed you?

388
00:24:55,894 --> 00:24:56,918
I demand order!

389
00:24:57,062 --> 00:24:58,690
Who paid you off?

390
00:24:58,831 --> 00:25:01,824
Answer me, you slimy little rat!

391
00:25:11,710 --> 00:25:15,772
I think somebody paid that Bigelow
fellow to get up on the stand and lie.

392
00:25:15,914 --> 00:25:17,712
If the bailiff
hadn't been there,

393
00:25:17,850 --> 00:25:20,718
Ellis would have punched
Fred Bigelow's lights right out.

394
00:25:20,853 --> 00:25:23,448
Ha ha! I'd kind of
like to have seen that.

395
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:27,323
Are you positive Fred
Bigelow wasn't telling the truth?

396
00:25:27,459 --> 00:25:32,261
Guys like Ellis don't kill
people, they buy them.

397
00:25:32,398 --> 00:25:34,765
And I don't think
Ellis bought anybody.

398
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:38,064
Did you talk to Miles
Turner's grandmother?

399
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,637
She confirmed his alibi.

400
00:25:39,772 --> 00:25:42,765
Says he came to
her house around 7

401
00:25:42,908 --> 00:25:47,243
and, in her words, spent the next
three hours with her at the theater,

402
00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:50,349
fawning and groveling
like a sniveling toad.

403
00:25:51,617 --> 00:25:53,142
What about the other two?

404
00:25:53,285 --> 00:25:55,325
I'm on my way to Tom
Neville's restaurant right now.

405
00:25:55,354 --> 00:25:58,688
How about dropping a
toothbrush off for Ellis on your way?

406
00:25:58,824 --> 00:26:00,258
Sure. Where is he at?

407
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:03,089
In jail. Contempt, you know.

408
00:26:10,836 --> 00:26:12,327
What's that you're
cooking there?

409
00:26:12,471 --> 00:26:17,739
Sautéed duck liver with Porcini
mushrooms and a little brandy.

410
00:26:17,876 --> 00:26:22,371
You could pour a quart of
brandy on it. Liver is still liver to me.

411
00:26:22,514 --> 00:26:23,538
What else have you got?

412
00:26:23,682 --> 00:26:26,311
Do you mind? I'm a
little too busy to chat.

413
00:26:27,553 --> 00:26:29,988
- I hear the food here is great.
- It is.

414
00:26:30,122 --> 00:26:31,681
Do you like working here?

415
00:26:31,824 --> 00:26:33,554
I own this restaurant.

416
00:26:33,692 --> 00:26:35,661
You do? What do you make best?

417
00:26:35,794 --> 00:26:38,161
Look, I'm not even
going to cook here tonight.

418
00:26:38,297 --> 00:26:39,297
Ann.

419
00:26:39,364 --> 00:26:41,060
Darn, that's bad luck.

420
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,793
Well, when are you here?

421
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:44,927
Every night but Wednesday.

422
00:26:45,070 --> 00:26:47,699
Look, you ought to
tell me where you work

423
00:26:47,840 --> 00:26:50,469
so I can come down and
talk to you when you're busy.

424
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:52,976
I'd like that. Morgan's
Mortuary on Peachtree.

425
00:26:53,112 --> 00:26:55,308
I should have known.

426
00:28:11,089 --> 00:28:15,493
Hi. My name is Tom,
and I'm an alcoholic.

427
00:28:15,627 --> 00:28:17,493
Hi, Tom.

428
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:30,608
Are you still here?

429
00:28:30,742 --> 00:28:32,677
Yeah. Do you have a minute?

430
00:28:32,811 --> 00:28:34,712
Sure? What's the problem?

431
00:28:34,846 --> 00:28:36,405
So far, so good.

432
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:40,918
I just wanted to tell you how much your
advice and your support have meant to me.

433
00:28:41,053 --> 00:28:43,989
Oh, that's sweet, but I
haven't done anything special.

434
00:28:44,122 --> 00:28:45,647
Oh, of course you have.

435
00:28:45,791 --> 00:28:48,351
Isn't there something
I can do for you?

436
00:28:49,895 --> 00:28:53,354
Well, as a matter
of fact, there is.

437
00:28:53,498 --> 00:28:59,529
You just go into that courtroom and
do the best you can and win this case.

438
00:28:59,671 --> 00:29:01,333
That will be plenty.

439
00:29:04,042 --> 00:29:05,271
Thanks.

440
00:29:06,445 --> 00:29:08,812
I'm so proud of you.

441
00:29:10,048 --> 00:29:11,744
I really am.

442
00:29:15,821 --> 00:29:18,985
Lieutenant Brooks, did I
call you yesterday afternoon?

443
00:29:19,124 --> 00:29:20,148
Yes, you did.

444
00:29:20,292 --> 00:29:21,954
What was the nature
of our conversation?

445
00:29:22,094 --> 00:29:24,723
You wanted to know if the money
found in Jeff Holden's townhouse

446
00:29:24,863 --> 00:29:26,661
had been analyzed
for fingerprints.

447
00:29:26,798 --> 00:29:30,667
It hadn't, so I sent
it out for lab tests.

448
00:29:30,802 --> 00:29:33,169
- Do you have the results of these tests?
- Yes, I do.

449
00:29:33,305 --> 00:29:35,206
Would you tell the
court what they are?

450
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:39,277
The lab found the defendant's
fingerprints on three $50 bills.

451
00:29:39,411 --> 00:29:40,902
- What?
- Ellis, hold it.

452
00:29:41,046 --> 00:29:43,391
That's impossible! I never saw
that money, let alone touch it.

453
00:29:43,415 --> 00:29:45,145
Mr. Blake, sit
down and be quiet!

454
00:29:45,284 --> 00:29:47,082
What the hell is
going on around here?

455
00:29:47,219 --> 00:29:50,121
Your Honor, could I have a
moment with my client in private?

456
00:29:50,255 --> 00:29:53,089
You do that, Mr. Matlock,
because one more outburst like that,

457
00:29:53,225 --> 00:29:55,194
you'll both be
spending the night in jail.

458
00:29:55,327 --> 00:29:57,796
Court will recess
for 15 minutes.

459
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:03,425
I don't believe this.

460
00:30:03,568 --> 00:30:05,161
I'm still being set up.

461
00:30:05,304 --> 00:30:06,602
When is it going to stop?

462
00:30:06,738 --> 00:30:08,978
And when are you going to
start doing something about it?

463
00:30:09,074 --> 00:30:11,236
There's nothing I can do, Ellis.

464
00:30:11,376 --> 00:30:13,845
What the hell kind
of an answer is that?

465
00:30:17,549 --> 00:30:19,177
You don't believe me anymore.

466
00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:22,777
It doesn't matter what I believe.
The jury doesn't believe you.

467
00:30:22,921 --> 00:30:26,915
The evidence is stacked
against you... I'm talking stacked.

468
00:30:28,026 --> 00:30:29,221
You want me to plead guilty?

469
00:30:29,361 --> 00:30:31,125
No.

470
00:30:31,263 --> 00:30:34,791
I want to see if I can
cut a deal for you.

471
00:30:34,933 --> 00:30:38,665
If this thing goes before
the jury, we're going to lose.

472
00:30:38,804 --> 00:30:39,804
No!

473
00:30:39,871 --> 00:30:41,635
You've got to face facts.

474
00:30:41,773 --> 00:30:44,675
The fact is I didn't
do it. I'm innocent.

475
00:30:45,977 --> 00:30:47,445
Now put me on the stand.

476
00:30:47,579 --> 00:30:49,207
No, that's a bad idea.

477
00:30:49,348 --> 00:30:51,442
I'm going on the stand
whether you like it or not.

478
00:30:51,583 --> 00:30:53,779
I don't like it. No.
You'll hang yourself.

479
00:30:53,919 --> 00:30:56,411
I don't give a damn!
I'm going on the stand.

480
00:30:59,191 --> 00:31:02,389
You're my lawyer,
put me on the stand.

481
00:31:02,527 --> 00:31:08,467
Mr. Blake, did you go see Jeff
Holden on the 23rd of last month?

482
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:10,364
Yes, I did. I drove
to his townhouse.

483
00:31:10,502 --> 00:31:13,131
I wanted to talk to him about
his relationship with my daughter.

484
00:31:13,271 --> 00:31:16,139
- Did you speak with him?
- No. I never went inside.

485
00:31:16,274 --> 00:31:18,505
I turned around before I
even got to his front door.

486
00:31:21,580 --> 00:31:25,312
Did you... kill Jeff Holden?

487
00:31:25,450 --> 00:31:27,316
No, I did not.

488
00:31:29,955 --> 00:31:31,548
This is your gun, isn't it?

489
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:34,250
Yes. I kept it in the glove
compartment of my car.

490
00:31:34,393 --> 00:31:36,794
Do you always
remember to lock your car?

491
00:31:36,928 --> 00:31:38,419
No. In fact, I rarely remember.

492
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:42,762
So someone could have stolen
this gun from your glove compartment,

493
00:31:42,901 --> 00:31:45,803
used it to kill Jeff Holden,
and then put it back in your car?

494
00:31:45,937 --> 00:31:47,235
Easily.

495
00:31:47,372 --> 00:31:49,136
Thank you, Mr. Blake.

496
00:31:49,274 --> 00:31:50,902
Miss Richmond?

497
00:31:51,042 --> 00:31:52,670
Thank you, Your Honor.

498
00:31:57,015 --> 00:32:00,076
I'm sorry, Mr. Blake,
if I sound confused,

499
00:32:00,218 --> 00:32:03,416
but didn't you originally tell the
police that on the night of the murder

500
00:32:03,555 --> 00:32:06,150
you were in your car, driving
home from a golf tournament?

501
00:32:06,291 --> 00:32:07,554
No.

502
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:11,557
- So you lied before?
- Well... Yes or no?

503
00:32:11,696 --> 00:32:16,157
Did you or did you not lie to the police
regarding your whereabouts that night?

504
00:32:17,202 --> 00:32:20,229
Yes. But I never
went inside. I...

505
00:32:20,372 --> 00:32:22,637
Oh, yes, you went inside.

506
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:27,041
You went inside to deliver
the $10,000 you'd promised him

507
00:32:27,179 --> 00:32:29,011
if he left your daughter
alone. Didn't you?

508
00:32:29,147 --> 00:32:30,547
No, I didn't.

509
00:32:30,682 --> 00:32:32,627
Then how did your fingerprints
get on that money, Mr. Blake?

510
00:32:32,651 --> 00:32:33,949
I don't know.

511
00:32:34,085 --> 00:32:37,146
Didn't you give the money to Jeff
Holden, argue with him, then shoot him?

512
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:38,348
No!

513
00:32:38,490 --> 00:32:42,018
Then how did a bullet from your
gun wind up in his heart, Mr. Blake?

514
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:43,423
I don't know. Somebody stole...

515
00:32:43,562 --> 00:32:45,724
And after you shot him,
you ran out the back door,

516
00:32:45,864 --> 00:32:48,197
and maybe you reached into
your pocket for your car keys,

517
00:32:48,333 --> 00:32:50,035
and in the process,
one of the ball markers

518
00:32:50,059 --> 00:32:51,826
that were in your
pocket fell to the ground.

519
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:54,735
I didn't shoot him, though
God knows I felt like it.

520
00:32:54,873 --> 00:32:57,452
And I didn't run out the back door
because I never got to the front door.

521
00:32:57,476 --> 00:32:59,672
And I didn't leave a ball
marker on the ground!

522
00:32:59,811 --> 00:33:02,042
I had three of them,
and I've still got three.

523
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:04,649
- Maybe you replaced it, huh, Mr. Blake?
- No!

524
00:33:04,783 --> 00:33:08,379
That was your marker outside
the back door, wasn't it, Mr. Blake?

525
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:09,818
I was set up, damn it.

526
00:33:09,955 --> 00:33:12,220
The money. The gun. The marker.

527
00:33:12,357 --> 00:33:14,189
Somebody used it to set me up.

528
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:16,318
I didn't do it!

529
00:33:22,601 --> 00:33:25,537
You were spotted at
the scene of the crime.

530
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:27,536
Your gun did the killing.

531
00:33:27,672 --> 00:33:29,937
Your money... Your
fingerprints were on it.

532
00:33:30,075 --> 00:33:33,204
Your ball marker at
the foot of the steps.

533
00:33:37,382 --> 00:33:39,214
Ladies and gentlemen,

534
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:42,549
I'm afraid this man is
fighting a losing battle.

535
00:33:44,055 --> 00:33:45,216
Thank you, Your Honor.

536
00:33:58,637 --> 00:34:02,875
We find the defendant,
Ellis Blake, guilty.

537
00:34:05,677 --> 00:34:08,146
Thank you, ladies and
gentlemen of the jury.

538
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:12,081
You are dismissed, and the
defendant is remanded to custody.

539
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:15,449
Sentencing will be in this
court on the 17th of next month.

540
00:34:15,587 --> 00:34:17,647
Court is now in recess.

541
00:34:19,090 --> 00:34:20,649
We've got to appeal.

542
00:34:20,792 --> 00:34:21,816
Okay.

543
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:23,986
I'm innocent. I didn't kill him.

544
00:34:24,129 --> 00:34:27,258
You've got to do something.

545
00:34:27,399 --> 00:34:29,459
Well, don't just stand
there! Do something!

546
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:34,031
I'm sorry, Ellis. I truly am.

547
00:35:03,201 --> 00:35:04,601
Higher. Higher over there.

548
00:35:04,736 --> 00:35:06,329
- Perfect. Perfect.
- Right there?

549
00:35:11,910 --> 00:35:13,105
Thank you.

550
00:35:13,244 --> 00:35:15,076
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

551
00:35:16,581 --> 00:35:18,277
Shh, shh, shh, shh, shh.

552
00:35:25,590 --> 00:35:26,614
Hi.

553
00:35:26,758 --> 00:35:27,885
It's all clear.

554
00:35:28,026 --> 00:35:29,392
- Hi.
- Hi.

555
00:35:29,527 --> 00:35:31,428
I'm looking for Lauren Richmond.

556
00:35:31,563 --> 00:35:35,056
She's not here right now.
Can I help you with something?

557
00:35:35,200 --> 00:35:37,396
No. It's personal.

558
00:35:37,535 --> 00:35:40,835
She's due back in a half
hour. You're welcome to wait.

559
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:44,602
We're throwing a
little party for her.

560
00:35:44,743 --> 00:35:47,804
Could you just tell her that
Peter Vanderhoff is in town?

561
00:35:47,946 --> 00:35:48,970
Sure.

562
00:35:50,415 --> 00:35:52,008
How do you spell that?

563
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:55,143
V-A-N-D-E-R-H-O-F-F.

564
00:35:55,286 --> 00:35:57,517
- And you know her?
- Yeah.

565
00:35:57,656 --> 00:35:59,921
We had a drink down
in Columbus last week.

566
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:05,092
Just tell her I'll try
to catch her later.

567
00:36:05,230 --> 00:36:06,230
Thanks.

568
00:36:20,512 --> 00:36:22,913
Ben? Hi.

569
00:36:23,048 --> 00:36:24,175
Listen, if you're not busy,

570
00:36:24,315 --> 00:36:27,183
I wondered if you could take
a drive with me to Columbus.

571
00:36:28,620 --> 00:36:31,089
The Briarcrest Country Club.

572
00:36:33,358 --> 00:36:36,294
Therefore, Your Honor,
the defense moves

573
00:36:36,428 --> 00:36:39,921
that the guilty verdict
against Ellis Blake be set aside

574
00:36:40,065 --> 00:36:44,127
on the basis of
prosecutorial misconduct.

575
00:36:44,269 --> 00:36:46,033
This is an outrage.

576
00:36:46,171 --> 00:36:49,232
There was no misconduct
on the part of the prosecution.

577
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:52,606
Well, Mr. Matlock seems to
feel he can prove there was.

578
00:36:52,744 --> 00:36:57,011
He's wasting the court's time, to
say nothing of impugning my integrity.

579
00:36:57,148 --> 00:36:59,708
If I may be blunt, Your Honor,
this merely demonstrates

580
00:36:59,851 --> 00:37:03,481
that Mr. Matlock is nothing
more than a sore loser.

581
00:37:03,621 --> 00:37:05,783
Well, this is unusual,
I'll grant you that.

582
00:37:05,924 --> 00:37:08,723
But I'm willing to allow him
some leeway in this matter.

583
00:37:08,860 --> 00:37:10,021
But, Your Honor...

584
00:37:10,161 --> 00:37:14,758
At his request, I've compelled all
the original witnesses to appear.

585
00:37:14,899 --> 00:37:19,064
Now, Mr. Matlock, you have
one hour of the court's time,

586
00:37:19,204 --> 00:37:23,232
but mind you, if I detect so
much as a whiff of sour grapes,

587
00:37:23,374 --> 00:37:26,902
it may be the last hour you'll
spend in court for a long time.

588
00:37:27,045 --> 00:37:29,571
Yes, sir. Thank you.

589
00:37:29,714 --> 00:37:33,617
The defense calls
Mr. Dennis Frye to the stand.

590
00:37:44,329 --> 00:37:46,207
Do you swear to tell
the truth, the whole truth,

591
00:37:46,231 --> 00:37:47,641
and nothing but the
truth, so help you God?

592
00:37:47,665 --> 00:37:48,665
I do.

593
00:37:48,733 --> 00:37:50,361
- State your name, please.
- Dennis Frye.

594
00:37:50,502 --> 00:37:51,595
- Be seated.
- Thank you.

595
00:37:51,736 --> 00:37:56,037
Mr. Frye, would you please tell
the court what you do for a living?

596
00:37:56,174 --> 00:37:59,008
I manage the pro shop at
the Briarcrest Country Club.

597
00:37:59,144 --> 00:38:03,582
That's where they held their
invitational golf tournament last month.

598
00:38:03,715 --> 00:38:05,013
Yes, it is.

599
00:38:05,150 --> 00:38:06,482
Now, tell me, Mr. Frye,

600
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:13,388
uh, have you ever seen this
young lady down there before?

601
00:38:13,525 --> 00:38:15,494
Yes, I have.

602
00:38:15,627 --> 00:38:17,425
I never forget a customer.

603
00:38:17,562 --> 00:38:19,224
She came into your shop?

604
00:38:19,364 --> 00:38:21,094
Mm-hmm. During the tournament.

605
00:38:21,232 --> 00:38:23,098
Didn't buy much, though.

606
00:38:23,234 --> 00:38:25,396
Do you remember what she bought?

607
00:38:25,537 --> 00:38:27,836
A souvenir ball marker.

608
00:38:30,308 --> 00:38:32,277
One ball marker?

609
00:38:33,611 --> 00:38:35,079
That's it?

610
00:38:35,213 --> 00:38:39,981
Well, it struck me as kind of strange,
too. That's why it stuck in my mind.

611
00:38:40,118 --> 00:38:42,917
Did the date she bought
it stick in your mind?

612
00:38:43,054 --> 00:38:46,821
Mm-hmm. The last day of
the tournament... the 24th.

613
00:38:46,958 --> 00:38:52,920
Your Honor, I submit
that Miss Richmond knew

614
00:38:53,064 --> 00:38:59,026
that my client had three souvenir
golf ball markers in his pocket

615
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,401
when he was arrested
for contempt of court,

616
00:39:01,539 --> 00:39:06,375
and the marker she bought and
planted outside Jeff Holden's apartment

617
00:39:06,511 --> 00:39:11,313
was put there to further
implicate my client in his murder.

618
00:39:11,449 --> 00:39:14,783
That is an extremely
serious allegation.

619
00:39:14,919 --> 00:39:16,444
Miss Richmond?

620
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:20,590
I absolutely deny
this, Your Honor,

621
00:39:20,725 --> 00:39:24,662
and I caution Mr. Matlock that
these false statements are unethical

622
00:39:24,796 --> 00:39:28,096
and may subject him to
disciplinary action by the state bar.

623
00:39:28,233 --> 00:39:29,394
Mr. Matlock?

624
00:39:29,534 --> 00:39:31,901
I'd like to continue,
if I may, Your Honor.

625
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:32,765
Proceed.

626
00:39:32,904 --> 00:39:35,601
The defense would
like to excuse Mr. Frye.

627
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:37,800
- Thank you.
- You may step down.

628
00:39:37,942 --> 00:39:40,605
And call Mr. Stanton
Avery to the stand.

629
00:39:40,745 --> 00:39:42,737
Do you swear to tell
the truth, the whole truth,

630
00:39:42,881 --> 00:39:44,358
and nothing but the
truth, so help you God?

631
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:45,941
- I do.
- State your name, please.

632
00:39:46,084 --> 00:39:48,144
- Stanton Avery.
- Be seated.

633
00:39:49,153 --> 00:39:53,420
Uh, Jeff Holden was
blackmailing you, wasn't he?

634
00:39:53,558 --> 00:39:55,026
- Yes, he was.
- Why?

635
00:39:55,159 --> 00:39:59,392
Because he found out that I was
seeing the wife of a friend of mine.

636
00:39:59,530 --> 00:40:02,022
So you were paying him
to keep his mouth shut.

637
00:40:02,166 --> 00:40:03,166
Yes.

638
00:40:03,301 --> 00:40:04,963
I bet he was bleeding you dry.

639
00:40:06,304 --> 00:40:07,304
Very dry.

640
00:40:07,372 --> 00:40:09,273
And that's why you killed him?

641
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:11,535
I did no such thing.

642
00:40:11,676 --> 00:40:14,077
I was with my friend's
wife at that time.

643
00:40:14,212 --> 00:40:15,544
No, you weren't.

644
00:40:15,680 --> 00:40:19,549
She was with her husband at an
Anonymous meeting that evening...

645
00:40:19,684 --> 00:40:22,745
The same as every
Wednesday evening.

646
00:40:22,887 --> 00:40:24,014
Your Honor, I object.

647
00:40:24,155 --> 00:40:26,715
Mr. Matlock is
misleading this court.

648
00:40:26,858 --> 00:40:29,760
He says he's trying to prove
prosecutorial misconduct,

649
00:40:29,894 --> 00:40:32,523
but all he's really doing
is retrying his case.

650
00:40:32,664 --> 00:40:37,329
I must admit I'm not entirely comfortable
with this line of questioning, Mr. Matlock.

651
00:40:37,468 --> 00:40:39,266
I'm sorry, Your
Honor. I'll move on.

652
00:40:39,404 --> 00:40:42,841
Would you tell the court,
please, who Karen Brown is?

653
00:40:42,974 --> 00:40:44,943
I don't believe I know
any Karen Brown.

654
00:40:45,076 --> 00:40:46,076
Well, sure you do.

655
00:40:46,177 --> 00:40:50,740
She's the vice president at the Greater
Atlanta Bank where you do your banking.

656
00:40:50,882 --> 00:40:53,943
She's the one who
helps you out, you know,

657
00:40:54,085 --> 00:40:56,316
so you won't have to stand
in line like everyone else.

658
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:58,548
- Yes, yes. That Karen Brown.
- Yeah, yeah.

659
00:40:58,690 --> 00:41:02,718
When I asked the police to
do a full fingerprint analysis

660
00:41:02,860 --> 00:41:05,830
of all the money that was
found at the scene of the crime,

661
00:41:05,964 --> 00:41:10,766
whose fingerprints do you think
they found on almost all the bills?

662
00:41:10,902 --> 00:41:12,632
I have no idea.

663
00:41:12,770 --> 00:41:15,740
Karen Brown's. Karen Brown's.

664
00:41:15,873 --> 00:41:18,502
Because that's where
the money came from...

665
00:41:18,643 --> 00:41:22,444
Not from my client's
bank, but from yours.

666
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:28,451
Her fingerprints were found
on every single bill but three...

667
00:41:28,586 --> 00:41:36,016
Three 50s on which my client's
fingerprints so conveniently were found.

668
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:38,391
Why this discrepancy?

669
00:41:40,264 --> 00:41:44,725
While he was in jail
for contempt of court,

670
00:41:44,869 --> 00:41:51,002
somebody went through the envelope
containing my client's possessions

671
00:41:51,142 --> 00:41:54,977
and removed three
50s from his money clip

672
00:41:55,113 --> 00:41:58,481
and replaced them with
three 50s of her own,

673
00:41:58,616 --> 00:42:00,608
then went into
the evidence room,

674
00:42:00,752 --> 00:42:04,689
removed three 50s from the money
found at the scene of the crime,

675
00:42:04,822 --> 00:42:09,556
replaced them with three
50s belonging to my client

676
00:42:09,694 --> 00:42:13,563
so that his fingerprints
could be found on them.

677
00:42:15,033 --> 00:42:17,366
Now, who did this?

678
00:42:17,502 --> 00:42:20,995
Deputy D.A. Lauren
Richmond, of course.

679
00:42:21,139 --> 00:42:23,404
Can you substantiate this?

680
00:42:25,009 --> 00:42:26,500
Look here, Your Honor.

681
00:42:28,646 --> 00:42:31,309
She signed into
booking on the 24th,

682
00:42:31,449 --> 00:42:34,817
signed into the evidence
room on the 25th.

683
00:42:34,952 --> 00:42:38,787
And I'm sure if we had a
heart-to-heart talk with Mr. Fred Bigelow,

684
00:42:38,923 --> 00:42:44,988
we would discover that Miss Richmond
is responsible for his testimony, too.

685
00:42:47,598 --> 00:42:49,567
The first thing you did

686
00:42:49,700 --> 00:42:56,106
after you overheard my client
trying to buy off Jeff Holden

687
00:42:56,240 --> 00:43:03,545
was go to your bank and have your
friend Karen count you out $10,000 in 50s.

688
00:43:03,681 --> 00:43:06,879
Then you stole Ellis' gun
from the glove compartment

689
00:43:07,018 --> 00:43:08,714
where you knew
he always kept it.

690
00:43:08,853 --> 00:43:14,315
You figured he would be driving back
from the golf tournament in Columbus

691
00:43:14,459 --> 00:43:15,518
and wouldn't have an alibi

692
00:43:15,660 --> 00:43:20,689
so you went to Jeff Holden's
house and shot him with Ellis' gun.

693
00:43:20,832 --> 00:43:27,102
Then later that night, you replaced
Ellis' gun to the glove compartment.

694
00:43:28,139 --> 00:43:31,576
And Ellis helped you himself

695
00:43:31,709 --> 00:43:35,077
by lying about where he
was at the time of the murder.

696
00:43:35,213 --> 00:43:38,706
But Miss Richmond is wrong.

697
00:43:40,251 --> 00:43:42,516
My client is not guilty.

698
00:43:42,653 --> 00:43:44,144
You are.

699
00:43:48,192 --> 00:43:51,128
Your Honor, I ask the
court's permission to speak.

700
00:43:51,262 --> 00:43:52,491
Yes, you have it.

701
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:56,897
In view of the behavior of
my associate Miss Richmond,

702
00:43:57,034 --> 00:44:00,766
I am replacing her as of
now, if it pleases the court.

703
00:44:00,905 --> 00:44:02,965
It does.

704
00:44:03,107 --> 00:44:06,646
Miss Richmond, as you
well know, obstruction

705
00:44:06,670 --> 00:44:09,343
of justice is a
criminal offense.

706
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:11,779
You have jeopardized
your entire career.

707
00:44:11,916 --> 00:44:13,612
Have you anything to say?

708
00:44:21,325 --> 00:44:26,992
Your Honor, I was just so tired
of seeing guilty men go free,

709
00:44:27,131 --> 00:44:30,295
and there was so much real
evidence against Ellis Blake,

710
00:44:30,434 --> 00:44:32,426
I was certain he was guilty.

711
00:44:33,938 --> 00:44:37,966
I know I did wrong, but I
thought it was for the right reason.

712
00:44:38,109 --> 00:44:41,045
Miss Richmond, I am ordering
all the evidence against you

713
00:44:41,179 --> 00:44:44,115
forwarded to the proper
authorities for further investigation.

714
00:44:44,248 --> 00:44:47,582
Your Honor, the state would
like to join with the defense

715
00:44:47,718 --> 00:44:51,587
in asking for a judgment
notwithstanding the verdict

716
00:44:51,722 --> 00:44:55,181
and dismissal of all
charges against Ellis Blake.

717
00:44:55,326 --> 00:44:57,090
So ordered.

718
00:44:57,228 --> 00:45:00,323
Bailiff, take the
witness into custody.

719
00:45:00,464 --> 00:45:06,404
Mr. Blake, you are hereby dismissed
with this court's profound apologies.

720
00:45:08,072 --> 00:45:10,473
And we are dismissed.

721
00:45:10,608 --> 00:45:12,338
That's it? It's over?

722
00:45:12,476 --> 00:45:13,569
It's over.

723
00:45:14,679 --> 00:45:17,274
You're innocent, and it's over.

724
00:45:17,415 --> 00:45:18,747
Thank you, Ben.

725
00:45:24,589 --> 00:45:26,251
I'm sorry.

726
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:28,018
Me, too.

727
00:45:28,159 --> 00:45:30,788
I was just under
so much pressure

728
00:45:30,928 --> 00:45:34,365
going up against the famous Ben
Matlock my first time out the gate,

729
00:45:34,498 --> 00:45:37,161
I guess I just kind of lost it.

730
00:45:37,301 --> 00:45:39,736
You know, flipped
out temporarily.

731
00:45:39,870 --> 00:45:41,998
I mean, you could tell
them that, couldn't you?

732
00:45:42,139 --> 00:45:45,473
That I didn't really know what I was
doing and that I deserve another chance?

733
00:45:45,610 --> 00:45:47,943
I don't think so.

734
00:45:58,623 --> 00:46:00,489
I trusted her.

735
00:46:00,625 --> 00:46:02,150
I trusted her, too.

736
00:46:02,293 --> 00:46:03,852
Well, I feel like a fool.

737
00:46:03,995 --> 00:46:09,935
Well, I trusted her because
of what she said she was,

738
00:46:10,067 --> 00:46:13,094
but she sure proved
otherwise, didn't she?

739
00:46:13,237 --> 00:46:16,765
You mean innocent
until proven guilty?

740
00:46:16,907 --> 00:46:19,035
Where have I heard that before?

741
00:46:19,176 --> 00:46:20,508
Dag-gone if I know,

742
00:46:20,645 --> 00:46:23,911
but if you'll buy me a big
supper, maybe we can talk it over.

743
00:46:24,048 --> 00:46:25,346
Let's go.

